ogles2: EXT_draw_buffers on VC4's one colour buffer (docs/PI3_PLAN.md §2.1).
The fragment key gets draw_buffer: gl_FragData[draw_buffer] is the colour
(output setup and the blending in the shader), gl_FragColor in every pass;
ogles2.library draws a framebuffer with N attachments in N passes, one
variant each. v3dglslc sets it through vc4_draw_buffer while it compiles a
program's variants for gl_FragData[1..3]. Applies after 0015. Off (0),
nothing changes.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/vc4/vc4_qir.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/vc4/vc4_qir.h
@@ -332,6 +332,11 @@
         bool sample_alpha_to_coverage;
         bool sample_alpha_to_one;
         uint8_t logicop_func;
+        /* ogles2 (docs/PI3_PLAN.md §2.1, EXT_draw_buffers on one colour
+         * buffer): the output gl_FragData[draw_buffer] is the colour; the
+         * library draws a framebuffer with N attachments in N passes.
+         * gl_FragColor is the colour in every pass. */
+        uint8_t draw_buffer;
         uint32_t point_sprite_mask;
         uint32_t ubo_1_size;
         uint8_t ucp_enables;
